[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Electrical Subsystem: Optical PPG
VERSION: @GIT_BRANCH

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
**Scope**: The optical PPG subsystem includes the AFE and the optical module

**Optical module**: The optical module is the opto-mechanical interface between the users skin and the device

**AFE**: The purpose of the AFE is to generate the optical module driving signals, as well as measuring the outputs of the optical module. It is "driving" the optical module, and acting as an interface between the optical module and the MCU.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-14
STATUS: Active
TITLE: PPG SNR
STATEMENT: >>>
From our simulations, the optical module/AFE must produce PPG signals that are at least 20dB SNR for the HRM and SPO2 software algorithms
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
For the algorithms to work well, there must be a good signal.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-15
STATUS: Active
TITLE: PPG sample rate
STATEMENT: >>>
The PPG subsystem shall be capable of 500hz sample rate
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
To meet the accuracy requirements, the PPG subsystem must be able to sample at a high enough rate to meet those requirements.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: MOE-001-003
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: MOE-001-011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-17
STATUS: Active
TITLE: AFE LED drive capability
STATEMENT: >>>
The AFE(s) shall be capable of driving at least 3 LEDs
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
For the SPO2 algorithm, the device must use more than 1 wavelength of light.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: MOE-001-011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-25
STATUS: Active
TITLE: AFE SNR
STATEMENT: >>>
The AFE shall have an SNR (PD current/output voltage) of greater than
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
PI = AC/DC -> AC_min = I_min * PI
SNR_DC = DC / noise. This is how small the noise is compared to the steady current.
SNR_Pulse = AC / noise. This is how small the noise is compared to the heartbeat = 20dB from REQ-14

Sub into SNR_Pulse
SNR_Pulse = (DC * PI) / noise = SNR_DC * PI

SNR_DC = (SNR_Pulse / PI) = (1/PI) * SNR_Pulse
Ratios add in dB land

SNR_DC (dB) = 20*log(1/PI) + SNR_Pulse (20 dB in this case)

Assuming PI 0.1%, SNR_DC = 80dB
<<<

[[/SECTION]]
